 "posts": [
  {
   "slug": "how-we-met",
   "title": "How We Met: A Borrowed Umbrella",
   "date": "2026-05-02T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "It was raining, the bus was late, and one of us had an umbrella big enough for two. Eight years later, we still argue about who offered first.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Clara says Theo offered. Theo says Clara simply stepped under the umbrella and started talking about the weather. Both of us agree it was raining very hard, that the number 9 bus was twenty minutes late, and that neither of us minded.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We talked about the rain, then about books, then about a terrible film we had both seen that week. When the bus finally came, we sat together. When it reached Clara's stop, she stayed on for three more.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>I missed my stop on purpose. I have never told him that until now.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Clara</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The umbrella, by the way, still lives by our front door. It has a broken spoke and a lot of sentimental value.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Thank you for being part of our story. We cannot wait to celebrate the next chapter with you.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "our-story"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "memories"
   ],
   "featured_media": "rain",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Aunt Marguerite",
     "email": "marguerite@example.com",
     "content": "I knew that umbrella was important! Can't wait for June.",
     "date": "2026-05-03T09:00:00"
    },
    {
     "author": "Sam",
     "email": "sam@example.com",
     "content": "Three extra stops. Legendary.",
     "date": "2026-05-03T21:10:00"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "the-proposal",
   "title": "The Proposal on the Lighthouse Steps",
   "date": "2026-06-14T19:00:00",
   "excerpt": "One hundred and twelve steps, one very windy evening and a ring that almost blew away. Theo tells the story of the question.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>I had planned everything: the walk along the cliffs, the picnic, the sunset from the top of the old lighthouse. I had not planned for the wind.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>By step eighty I was holding the ring box in my fist inside my pocket, terrified. By step one hundred and twelve, Clara was laughing so hard at my hair that I almost forgot what I was there to do.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>She said yes before I finished the question. I am still a little offended.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Theo</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We ate the picnic on the lighthouse steps, out of the wind, watching the light come on for the night. It was perfect, mostly because nothing went to plan.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:lighthouse}}\" alt=\"A lighthouse on a cliff at sunset\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The lighthouse at Gull Point, where it all happened.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->",
   "categories": [
    "our-story"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "memories",
    "proposal"
   ],
   "featured_media": "lighthouse",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "choosing-our-venue",
   "title": "Choosing Our Venue: Why The Orchard House",
   "date": "2026-07-20T11:00:00",
   "excerpt": "We visited nine venues and fell for the one with crooked apple trees, a stone barn and a long table under the branches.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We had a list of requirements: room for a hundred people, somewhere for the children to run, and a place that felt like us. The Orchard House ticked every box, and then added a few we had not thought of.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The ceremony</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Under the oldest apple tree, with the hills behind.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The dinner</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>One long table in the stone barn, lit by candles.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The dancing</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>On the terrace, until the stars come out and beyond.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If it rains, the ceremony moves into the barn, which is also beautiful, and drier.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:gallery {\"columns\":3,\"linkTo\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:venue}}\" alt=\"The stone barn at The Orchard House\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:table}}\" alt=\"A long table set for dinner\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:garden}}\" alt=\"The garden path to the orchard\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --></figure><!-- /wp:gallery -->",
   "categories": [
    "planning"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "venue"
   ],
   "featured_media": "venue",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "menu-tasting-day",
   "title": "Menu Tasting Day (We Ate Everything)",
   "date": "2026-08-15T14:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Six starters, four mains, three desserts and one very patient chef. Here is what made the menu, and what did not.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Menu tasting is, without question, the best part of wedding planning. We arrived hungry and left about four hours later, very full and slightly emotional about a lemon tart.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What made the menu</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Summer tomato salad with herbs from the orchard garden</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Slow-roasted lamb, or a wild mushroom pie for vegetarians</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Lemon tart with crème fraîche, of course</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A late-night cheese table for the dancers</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Please tell us about any allergies or dietary needs on your RSVP. The kitchen is wonderful and happy to adapt everything.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The cake, by the way, is still a secret. We have been sworn to silence by the baker, who takes these things very seriously.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "planning"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "food"
   ],
   "featured_media": "table",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Priya",
     "email": "priya.r@example.com",
     "content": "The lemon tart better be as good as it sounds!",
     "date": "2026-08-16T08:00:00"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "our-flowers",
   "title": "Our Flowers: Garden Roses and Wild Things",
   "date": "2026-09-05T10:30:00",
   "excerpt": "Blush garden roses, sweet peas, a little wild grass and as much greenery as the florist would allow.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We wanted the flowers to look as though someone had just walked through the orchard and picked them. Our florist understood immediately.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Blush garden roses and pale peonies</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Sweet peas in white and lilac</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Olive branches, wild grasses and trailing ivy</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>After the wedding, the table flowers will go home with guests and the rest to the care home down the lane. Nothing will be wasted.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Make it look like June.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Our only instruction to the florist</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->",
   "categories": [
    "planning"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "flowers"
   ],
   "featured_media": "bouquet",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "travel-and-stay-guide",
   "title": "Travel and Stay: A Guide for Our Guests",
   "date": "2026-09-25T09:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Trains, parking, the best places to stay nearby and the bus we have booked to take everyone home after the dancing.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Willowmere is a small village, so here is everything you need to know to arrive relaxed and leave happy.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Getting there</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>By train: Willowmere station is a ten-minute walk; we will have a shuttle at 13:30.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>By car: free parking at the venue; please car-share if you can.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Going home: a coach leaves at 23:30 for the station and the two hotels below.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Where to stay</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:table --><figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Place</th><th>Distance</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The Willow Inn</td><td>5 minutes</td><td>Rooms held for guests until March</td></tr><tr><td>Mill House B&amp;B</td><td>10 minutes</td><td>Lovely breakfasts</td></tr><tr><td>Station Hotel</td><td>15 minutes</td><td>Coach stops outside</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><!-- /wp:table --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Questions? Message either of us any time.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you are travelling from further away and would like help planning, just ask: we have favourite cafés, walks and a very good bakery to recommend.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "guest-info"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "travel"
   ],
   "featured_media": "garden",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "dress-code-explained",
   "title": "The Dress Code, Explained",
   "date": "2026-10-05T12:00:00",
   "excerpt": "\"Garden formal\" sounds mysterious. It mostly means: dress up, but wear shoes you can walk on grass in.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our invitations say garden formal. We have had several worried messages, so here is what we mean.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Yes, please</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Summer suits, linen, lighter colours</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Dresses of any length</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Comfortable shoes or block heels</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A layer for the evening</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Maybe not</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Stiletto heels (the lawn will win)</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Head-to-toe white</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Anything you would be sad to get a little grass on</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Most of all, wear something you feel happy in. That is the only rule that really matters.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>And if the evening turns cool, there will be blankets on the terrace and a basket of spare flat shoes by the dance floor.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "guest-info"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "dress-code"
   ],
   "featured_media": "invitation",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "meet-the-wedding-party",
   "title": "Meet the Wedding Party",
   "date": "2026-10-18T16:00:00",
   "excerpt": "The friends and family who will stand beside us, keep us calm and, almost certainly, give speeches we will never live down.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We are lucky to be surrounded by wonderful people. Here are the ones who will be standing next to us on the day.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Juno</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Clara's sister and maid of honour. In charge of tissues and timekeeping.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Felix</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Theo's oldest friend and best man. In charge of the rings, which worries everyone.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ada &amp; Leo</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our niece and nephew, flower girl and ring bearer. In charge of chaos.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you need anything on the day, find Juno. She will have a plan, a spare hair pin and probably a snack.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "wedding-party"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "friends"
   ],
   "featured_media": "rings",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  }
